  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Sec. 1, 2-4-108(e) (new)\n(quote) The coordinator of elections shall include in the educational standards created pursuant to subsection (a) training on temporary forms of identification issued to non-United States citizens that may not be used as evidence of identification as set forth in § 2-7-112(c).\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Draft (both copies): 2-2-134(c): records of purged voters kept 3 years instead of 2. Removed by the rewrite.\n(other) Chaptered Sec. 2: effective January 1, 2026.\n(other) version: 3104597-Draft (SB only): caption bill about retention of purged-voter records (2 to 3 years). No slot a-e text.\n(other) version: 3106252-Draft (adds House companion HB1283 header): same operative text as 3104597.\n(other) version: amend-245330-SA0325 (Senate State & Local Gov't amendment 1; 'adopted' flag 0, dated 2025-04-03; action log shows adoption 2025-04-15): deletes all after the enacting clause; substitutes the 2-4-108(e) training rule. Adds the slot a text.\n(other) version: 3236652-Chaptered (PC 394): same as SA0325.\n(other) note: Weak, implementation-only slot a: it adds no ID rule, only a training topic that points at the existing 2-7-112(c) list. The filed Draft has no ID text; the rewrite (SA0325) does, and all three roll calls were on the rewritten text (Draft + SA0325) as far as the log shows. The SA0325 file is dated one day after the 4/2 committee vote, so the committee-vote version is inferred.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
